WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.591
X-rays are produced when fast electrons from the cathode strike the tungsten target.

2
00:00:06.591 --> 00:00:12.676
Bremsstrahlung occurs when an electron is slowed or deflected near the nucleus.

3
00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:23.323
Characteristic radiation begins when an incoming electron removes an inner-shell electron, and a higher-shell electron fills the vacancy, releasing a photon.
